{"title":"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 24","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Diagram\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Diagram</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_6_(Proof)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6 (Proof)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_MOP_2024\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by MOP 2024</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> has right angles at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/5/7b50ae2c8646f49931c2e65cf58ca8625ebc4324.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC \\sim \\triangle BCD$\" width=\"143\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/5/235e58b6a077ef9b4e2372c3ea5b53ddbccffa59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB &gt; BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"81\" height=\"13\" />. There is a point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> in the interior of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/8/b5818cf5dba01fec955a95fb1c46961c128e7316.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC \\sim \\triangle CEB$\" width=\"142\" height=\"13\" /> and the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/1/18167d788fd698322ba516cf8bfdba2c931fa17d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AED$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/6/b7616a230c77f0d9a577e5bca01aa06f1c35c457.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> times the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/0/dd0941332df51be1f43d6d79c408718ff41b234e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle CEB$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" />. What is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/a/b3af6bbe780177f576e104b0cbc9af9d124f6bd7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{AB}{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"23\" height=\"21\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/9/b39e21d1d69b7c6158b090848229d967990426a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 1+\\sqrt{2} \\qquad \\textbf{(B) } 2 + \\sqrt{2} \\qquad \\textbf{(C) } \\sqrt{17} \\qquad \\textbf{(D) } 2 + \\sqrt{5} \\qquad \\textbf{(E) } 1 + 2\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"573\" height=\"21\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Diagram\">Diagram</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Diagram\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-center\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2017AMC12BP24.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/4/43/2017AMC12BP24.png/300px-2017AMC12BP24.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"300\" height=\"383\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/4/43/2017AMC12BP24.png/450px-2017AMC12BP24.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/4/43/2017AMC12BP24.png/600px-2017AMC12BP24.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/8/be87e1009c72fa27052808250c268f5603702144.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"62\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/e/7ce3e753b80409dd0bc8efe53bef3268617483a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC=x$\" width=\"63\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/9/ae9c125e6ef343c89b3e612128755953872cae4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=x^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"72\" height=\"17\" />. Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/d/0cde450acac2128432a3e68614d3ca368174c60d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB/BC=x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"100\" height=\"18\" />. By the Pythagorean Theorem, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/7/6874c50cd7acd7694ac9292ec4e6ee234af21d09.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD=\\sqrt{x^2+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"119\" height=\"18\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/0/e40fb7a1aaafde80a4c8ef2304701a3e4ef0b0a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BCD \\sim \\triangle ABC \\sim \\triangle CEB$\" width=\"227\" height=\"13\" />, the ratios of side lengths must be equal. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/e/7ce3e753b80409dd0bc8efe53bef3268617483a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC=x$\" width=\"63\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/4/4549989ade3859839c5263d15c675f7dedcba84c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CE=\\frac{x^2}{\\sqrt{x^2+1}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"119\" height=\"43\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/2/ec240210889bb2b3daafc732fa95efab108d5235.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BE=\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{x^2+1}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"120\" height=\"37\" />. Let F be a point on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e33fe7d65facd8868f58b6e94ddc7f153a5a3f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/0/ed0f6a692f19a65fe60fe5745826792f3fd1d57e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{EF}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> is an altitude of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/2/f52863fdb7628708d5fe508796064193c3aa12b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CEB$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />. Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/7/697329f94a7ed7c7261d8a2ff3ee71a2a22badc8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle CEB \\sim \\triangle CGE \\sim \\triangle EFB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"229\" height=\"18\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/3/303060d984b99f22146e6f3e2c660741313d03b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF=\\frac{x}{x^2+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"108\" height=\"36\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/8/51851fdb925f16a75400d68d433bf5807ff1cbee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EG=\\frac{x^3}{x^2+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"108\" height=\"42\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/7/bc7f4fd0e5897e8ac812a9a562556b8cdd87341f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{CF}$\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/a/0aa4ad1cf6a0ad719767e1739c9b689debc60142.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BF}$\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" /> form altitudes of triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/5/dc5309b25510f426ca00c957623bd0396c79e4c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CED$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/7/e07a934f110b579c0ee7451176a281ae64e8c426.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BEA$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />, respectively, the areas of these triangles can be calculated. Additionally, the area of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/1/ef14ba8fc495f2a5750a5ed394ebf75a28641658.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BEC$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> can be calculated, as it is a right triangle. Solving for each of these yields:\n</p><p>\\begin{align*}\n[BEC] &amp;=[CED]=[BEA]=\\frac{x^3}{2(x^2+1)} \\\\\n[ABCD] &amp;=[AED]+[DEC]+[CEB]+[BEA] \\\\\n\\frac{(BC)(AB+CD)}{2} &amp;= 17*[CEB]+ [CEB] + [CEB] + [CEB] \\\\\n\\frac{x^3+x}{2} &amp;= \\frac{20x^3}{2(x^2+1)} \\\\\n(x)(x^2+1) &amp;= \\frac{20x^3}{x^2+1} \\\\\n(x^2+1)^2 &amp;=20x^2 \\\\\nx^4-18x^2+1 &amp;=0 \\implies x^2=9+4\\sqrt{5}=4+2(2\\sqrt{5})+5 \\\\\n\\end{align*}\n</p><p>Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/6/b069a2d091f9fc11ef6eb31b8c5f49eb7f980e32.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } 2+\\sqrt{5}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"103\" height=\"33\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Draw line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/5/3951902c11a1cd39a091ea15f0f06cbc79095de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FG$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/e/79e63ce05526500aed397b865e811ce16dc214e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FG \\parallel AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"75\" height=\"19\" />. WLOG let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/8/be87e1009c72fa27052808250c268f5603702144.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"62\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/e/58ebecbda27d4895426680a28c173bf47c672c85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CB=x$\" width=\"63\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/9/ae9c125e6ef343c89b3e612128755953872cae4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=x^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"72\" height=\"17\" />. By weighted average <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/1/1c183e25d029ff640cac6702d4d0d3ca15672470.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FG=\\frac{1+x^4}{1+x^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"104\" height=\"40\" />. \n</p><p>Meanwhile, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/3/3636d885a9313e9c001ea09b6e7d00fdcbd9b7b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FE:EG=[\\triangle CBE]:[\\triangle ADE]=1:17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"318\" height=\"18\" />. This follows from comparing the ratios of triangle DEG to CFE and triangle AEG to FEB, both pairs in which the two triangles share a height perpendicular to FG, and have base ratio <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/3/403c5183c36e67c2430d3f6612eb94ad0f48fd0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EG:FE$\" width=\"72\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/8/44868246d4ef112a105aaf2c04baa2f35e908fc2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FE=\\frac{x^2}{1+x^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"104\" height=\"40\" />. We obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/a/b8a8812582e5f98f03569f47644b8ffaae3f701d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1+x^4}{1+x^2}=\\frac{18x^2}{1+x^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"129\" height=\"40\" />,\nnamely <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/9/3e911dbbfea91d9da6ca98a45870a55efb775e83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^4-18x^2+1=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"140\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>The rest is the same as Solution 1.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-center\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2017AMC12BP24.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/4/43/2017AMC12BP24.png/300px-2017AMC12BP24.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"300\" height=\"383\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/4/43/2017AMC12BP24.png/450px-2017AMC12BP24.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/4/43/2017AMC12BP24.png/600px-2017AMC12BP24.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/0/f80e67527934e0557de487e6fdc23ea439b269b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = a$\" width=\"62\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/d/a7d5f81f182d0b2c07569dfc7ce37b85d901cabf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC = b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"63\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/7/ee708b4ea750f06ae95a2ef332a150efcc25db62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC = \\sqrt{a^2+b^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"124\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> cannot be the intersection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fff82bb65d0215e49c8c91cb7c553da52205e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />, as that would mean <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/2/742be37c99b26a430078db218d62e8dc32ff30b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[AED] = [CEB]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"133\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/6/a466af836fddc38a2456ac1a110a0c7573bcaf94.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\because \\triangle BCD \\sim \\triangle ABC, \\quad \\therefore \\frac{CD}{BC} = \\frac{BC}{AB}, \\quad CD = BC \\cdot \\frac{BC}{AB} = b \\cdot \\frac{b}{a} = \\frac{b^2}{a}\\]\" width=\"537\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3e2df6e58bd77c71337fdba09fcbda1ebf800c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[[CEB] = ( \\frac{BC}{AC} )^2 \\cdot [ABC] = ( \\frac{b}{ \\sqrt{a^2+b^2} } )^2 \\cdot \\frac{ab}{2} = \\frac{ab^3}{2(a^2+b^2)}\\]\" width=\"454\" height=\"44\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/5/b451fab1ce6eb5383b1d42608c5b6e7285bb71f3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[BF = \\frac{ 2[CEB] }{BC} = \\frac{ 2 \\cdot \\frac{ab^3}{ 2(a^2+b^2) } }{b} = \\frac{ab^2}{a^2+b^2}\\]\" width=\"308\" height=\"47\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/1/ac1f05409a1f0809e456e286b79e9c8a5b947b4d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\because \\triangle BFE \\sim \\triangle ABC, \\quad \\therefore \\frac{EF}{BF} = \\frac{BC}{AB}, \\quad EF = BF \\cdot \\frac{BC}{AB} = \\frac{ab^2}{a^2+b^2} \\cdot \\frac{b}{a} = \\frac{b^3}{a^2+b^2}\\]\" width=\"617\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/5/5e59440bebea72177bbf99edfb0d42c31ecc2575.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[EG = FG - EF = b - \\frac{b^3}{a^2+b^2} = \\frac{a^2b}{a^2+b^2}\\]\" width=\"326\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/1/a9120effe4549761d901d0fdf165393062335966.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[[ABCD] = \\frac{AB + CD}{2} \\cdot BC = \\frac{a + \\frac{b^2}{a} }{2} \\cdot b = \\frac{ b(a^2+b^2) }{ 2a }\\]\" width=\"417\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/9/159027aae27afe6b759a61b7813ec8a3a216e7d3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[[ABE] = \\frac12 \\cdot AB \\cdot EF = \\frac12 \\cdot a \\cdot \\frac{b^3}{a^2+b^2} = \\frac{ab^3}{ 2(a^2+b^2) }\\]\" width=\"407\" height=\"44\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/6/736f780d627e85c31d3b3b585e9b08519100327e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[[CDE] = \\frac12 \\cdot CD \\cdot EG = \\frac12 \\cdot \\frac{a^2b}{a^2+b^2} \\cdot \\frac{a^2b}{a^2+b^2} = \\frac{ab^3}{ 2(a^2+b^2) }\\]\" width=\"459\" height=\"44\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/3/a036ed545d8489164176d31eb7097f3393351df5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[ADE = [ABCD] - [ABE] - [CEB] - [CDE] = \\frac{ b(a^2+b^2) }{ 2a } - \\frac{ab^3}{ 2(a^2+b^2) } - \\frac{ab^3}{ 2(a^2+b^2) }- \\frac{ab^3}{ 2(a^2+b^2) } = \\frac{ b(a^2+b^2)^2 - 3a^2b^3 }{ 2a(a^2+b^2) }\\]\" width=\"905\" height=\"44\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/c/b8c90c41b6f6c2741a097ad59143289b465fc935.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{ [ADE] }{ [CEB] } = \\frac { \\frac{ b(a^2+b^2)^2 - 3a^2b^3 }{ 2a(a^2+b^2) } }{ \\frac{ab^3}{2(a^2+b^2)} } = \\frac{  (a^2 + b^2)^2 - 3a^2b^2 }{ a^2b^2 } = \\frac{ a^4 - a^2b^2 + b^4 }{ a^2b^2 } = 17\\]\" width=\"537\" height=\"58\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/3/e230665702353024df2b91a15541f8663cfcb217.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a^4 - a^2b^2 + b^4 = 17 a^2b^2, \\quad a^4 + b^4 = 18 a^2b^2, \\quad \\frac{a^2}{b^2} + \\frac{b^2}{a^2} = 18\\]\" width=\"468\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/c/cbc6a9edffa29df6963235e8d1bdbbde4e49dd9b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\frac{a}{b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"46\" height=\"33\" />,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/c/64c640c721e1cf11c51e7e60fccd1097e6851622.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^2 + \\frac{1}{x^2} = 18, \\quad x^4 - 18x^2 + 1 = 0, \\quad x^2 = \\frac{18 + \\sqrt{324-4} }{2} = 9+ 4\\sqrt{5}\\]\" width=\"540\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/f/def7eddd1d370bfc495343756f2fd662194d1cab.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{a}{b} = \\sqrt{ 9+ 4\\sqrt{5} } = \\sqrt{ 4+ 4\\sqrt{5}+5 } = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } 2+ \\sqrt{5}}\\]\" width=\"383\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>~<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:Isabelchen\">isabelchen</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/9/96900e7970eacd9a992fed8bb0898a839ece09f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A=(-1,4a), B=(-1,0), C=(1,0), D=\\bigg(1,\\frac{1}{a}\\bigg)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"392\" height=\"43\" />. Then from the similar triangles condition, we compute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/3/7832a47bb0466e344509341a45f79343eef811d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CE=\\frac{4a}{\\sqrt{4a^2+1}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"128\" height=\"41\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/5/01521e4bf5e149d6708e13d3333048cd6b8401f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BE=\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{4a^2+1}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"128\" height=\"41\" />. Hence, the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-coordinate of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is just <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/e/08e7bf52048b004c45caa121f02d167f191d6bd6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{BE\\cdot CE}{BC}=\\frac{4a}{4a^2+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"159\" height=\"39\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> lies on the unit circle, we can compute the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> coordinate as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/b/10b41a81b4640d8846937a4d5b7bed729333d96f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1-4a^2}{4a^2+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"63\" height=\"42\" />. By Shoelace, we want <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/1/e31a4129613c976758006d351f412b52e389f462.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{2}\\det\\begin{bmatrix} -1 &amp; 4a &amp; 1\\\\  \\frac{1-4a^2}{4a^2+1} &amp; \\frac{4a}{4a^2+1} &amp; 1\\\\  1 &amp; \\frac{1}{a} &amp; 1 \\end{bmatrix}=17\\cdot\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2 \\cdot \\frac{4a}{4a^2+1}\\]\" width=\"354\" height=\"65\" />Factoring out denominators and expanding by minors, this is equivalent to\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/c/81c1d36defdc35cb83db1bc4d7acb1edeb135d67.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{32a^4-8a^2+2}{2a(4a^2+1)}=\\frac{68a}{4a^2+1} \\Longrightarrow 16a^4-72a^2+1=0\\]\" width=\"398\" height=\"43\" />This factors as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/e/3ee3a07baccb5b80df9fc8894f0067a47a1db320.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4a^2-8a-1)(4a^2+8a-1)=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"258\" height=\"19\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/3/e73eb65b2bb9e18c6cda5734c3dd40be65a9d9ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=1+\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"92\" height=\"41\" /> and so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/0/6708d8f91d31125a89b749916a8367c5cfa1572f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(D) \\ }$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"28\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/6/2d605ce852ce62c02c8d322cfe09980a8ebb3cfd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C = (0,0), D=\\left(\\frac1a, 0\\right), B = (0,1), A = (a,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"363\" height=\"45\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/8/eb8726d98aced2f3140dd77a2d8614c2e7674700.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />. Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/e/7aef3a8b18e2d8a4b29ca70301f3dbcfe9420593.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC = 1, a = \\frac{AB}{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"139\" height=\"39\" />. Notice that the diagonals are perpendicular with slopes of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/6/05682e1a6a5b425f381195377a580b000f4d27e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac1a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"12\" height=\"37\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/b/5ab0d6b0f629cdfba5b6ce68695ff0c5a2d6fd8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-a$\" width=\"23\" height=\"8\" />. Let the intersection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fff82bb65d0215e49c8c91cb7c553da52205e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/b/6dbe073e978e0e1fd7fab0405f8fb4602797382e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BFC \\sim \\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"144\" height=\"18\" />. However, because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is a trapezoid, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/9/009cf3eeb0ff3789cc057632947cadb200ab4663.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/a/89a3f0e3dd12e6a4cc523abc05db1a2bce99298d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BCF$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/7/3e728a789f2ca839593526b82229b72fde61ec6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ADF$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> share the same area, therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/9/009cf3eeb0ff3789cc057632947cadb200ab4663.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/2/91275aa1f85be8f39ea3ae3cef68f10100fc664b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BCE$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> is the reflection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/9/009cf3eeb0ff3789cc057632947cadb200ab4663.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/a/89a3f0e3dd12e6a4cc523abc05db1a2bce99298d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BCF$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> over the perpendicular bisector of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/d/c1d2e19a4a14e740d1d2b7b53b268e4d579d8619.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=\\frac12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"45\" height=\"37\" />. We use the linear equations of the diagonals, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/8/1e8f7dea008135f46d651326bf7e285e821bff5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = -ax + 1, y = \\frac1a x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"167\" height=\"38\" />, to find the coordinates of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/2/60210eaf10801fb8aa31aaf4e6f5d6e45aaa73c0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[-ax+1 = \\frac1ax \\Longrightarrow x = \\frac{1}{a+\\frac1a} = \\frac{a}{a^2+1}\\]\" width=\"307\" height=\"43\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/9/5c9a0701a3c96b8f8c545c702f2ed3b0c8f3638f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[y = \\frac1ax = \\frac{1}{a^2+1}\\]\" width=\"132\" height=\"38\" />\nThe y-coordinate of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is simply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/a/5ea70c6538023d944954a5a760fdd35941305309.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1-\\frac{1}{a^2+1} = \\frac{a^2}{a^2+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"162\" height=\"42\" />\nThe area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/3/423d2cdb9f74980709bf26fc4bb3cb0304964a8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BCE$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/c/a5c02648a963ce1f45dcd88aaf970b312426b498.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac12 \\left(\\frac{a}{a^2+1} \\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"96\" height=\"45\" />. We apply shoelace theorem to solve for the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/0/db041d9c0fda44cf24b4f4ae7f02243ef2ea7f92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ADE$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" />. The coordinates of the triangle are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/0/fa08a42957f48e3edbe9e4b5d5a25460c0c8453b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{(\\frac{a}{a^2+1}, \\frac{a^2}{a^2+1}), (a,1), (\\frac1a, 0)\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"249\" height=\"42\" />, so the area is \n</p><p>\\begin{equation}\n\\begin{split}\n\\frac12 \\left|\\frac{a^3}{a^2+1} + \\frac1a - \\frac{a}{a^2+1} - \\frac{a}{a^2+1}\\right| &amp; = \\frac12 \\left|\\frac{a^3-2a}{a^2+1} + \\frac1a \\right| \\\\\n&amp; = \\frac12 \\left|\\frac{a^4-2a^2}{a(a^2+1)} + \\frac{a^2+1}{a(a^2+1)} \\right| \\\\\n&amp; = \\frac12 \\left( \\frac{a^4-a^2+1}{a(a^2+1)}\\right).\n\\end{split}\n\\end{equation}\n</p><p>Finally, we use the property that the ratio of areas equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/6/b7616a230c77f0d9a577e5bca01aa06f1c35c457.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/2/1623e61a96070047eda686442fd663c2b9e1589b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\frac12\\left(\\frac{a^4-a^2+1}{a(a^2+1)}\\right)}{\\frac12\\left(\\frac{a}{a^2+1}\\right)} = 17 \\Rightarrow \\frac{a^4-a^2+1}{a^2} = 17 \\Rightarrow a^4-18a^2+1 = 0\\]\" width=\"467\" height=\"69\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/0/e700fc8007f7204e44f9552f5daf373710fc47d8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a^2 = 9+4\\sqrt{5} = (2+\\sqrt{5})^2 \\Longrightarrow a = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } 2+\\sqrt{5}}.\\]\" width=\"386\" height=\"33\" />\n</p><p>~Zeric\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_6_.28Proof.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6_(Proof)\">Solution 6 (Proof)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6 (Proof)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>This solution involves proving <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/0/230832bc38d0e005fbe9358b0ffc1326734c3d7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AED \\sim \\triangle CEB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"146\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/1/411ef29ce6c32ab71534dfd3319a6fe72af9c5ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E&#39;$\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> be the intersection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fff82bb65d0215e49c8c91cb7c553da52205e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />. Label points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> the same way as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/d/66d00efb754f567403b93840a038031c3aa46d9b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{Solution 3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"87\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/0/2001594e2d6a587ce79ad8335557d286dd809306.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AE&#39;D = \\angle CE&#39;B = \\frac{\\pi}{2} = \\angle AFE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"267\" height=\"34\" />. Additionally, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/4/9e41c184496cb4547dadbb630eca6e121a559a9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{E&#39;D}{FE} = \\frac{E&#39;D}{E&#39;G} = \\frac{AE&#39;}{AF}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"164\" height=\"40\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/7/527f64a6a4b394b9b5e3bc617a1451e344c31f5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AFE \\sim \\triangle AE&#39;D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"149\" height=\"19\" /> by SAS. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/b/d3bed67d256959c6db503abfe0264ee15074f0e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAC = \\angle FAE + \\angle EAE&#39; = \\angle E&#39;AD + \\angle EAE&#39; = \\angle EAD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"467\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nNext, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/7/7d77bb5d1b480e469ec7b27c02007ce59cc6dd50.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AFE = \\frac{\\pi}{2} = \\angle EGD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"178\" height=\"34\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/e/6ce4f349237ba7035bdeeb9463091de1b377dc9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FG \\parallel BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"79\" height=\"20\" />. Also, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/4/544339287fb4bfa1845df878fd4281b72bae957a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi = \\angle FEA + \\angle AED + \\angle DEG = \\angle FEA + \\angle AED + \\angle EAF = \\frac{\\pi}{2} + \\angle AED$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"604\" height=\"34\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/6/a06f4d700f702e5a77cfadf51c020f4c00d7d7bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AED = \\frac{\\pi}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"98\" height=\"34\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/c/1fc048d1d191847da8b9c72bca6934ebae688907.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AED \\sim \\triangle ABC$\" width=\"142\" height=\"13\" /> by AA. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/1/871dd47d980de5f6dbe1ae45456b26bcd2031edf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle CEB \\sim \\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"144\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/0/230832bc38d0e005fbe9358b0ffc1326734c3d7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AED \\sim \\triangle CEB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"146\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nGiven <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/c/f5caf402e30652960c640d2937bce5b0021b2c51.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{[AED]}{[CEB]} = 17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"102\" height=\"45\" />, we deduce that the ratio of corresponding side lengths of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/1/6f1bf55dee68ba4123ca736e3b4b2121ffebc98a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AED$\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/2/f52863fdb7628708d5fe508796064193c3aa12b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CEB$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/6/2a6847786e6937f02f810e74a056f4c8f289a931.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{17}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" />. Now, we set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/6/74666022a42f4446ed551033a088108882c5ec09.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/0/0a0bbad507209d4947c10a4c8ab5274bff49d568.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"65\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/1/241162e2de08266f37d05ef42dcc6ceb8848e3b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD = \\frac{1}{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"70\" height=\"38\" />. Using the Pythagorean Theorem, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee4bcced790e263cc22f16e83c2e9f70a332c69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD = \\sqrt{\\Big(x-\\frac{1}{x}\\Big)^2 + 1^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"187\" height=\"45\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/c/96c51744d47b253a9ebf46e89b9645bada7eda41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{17} = \\frac{AD}{CB} = \\frac{\\sqrt{\\Big(x-\\frac{1}{x}\\Big)^2 + 1^2}}{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"250\" height=\"65\" />. Solving gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/1/ef1f89250d16d3ba9e1c52e49eb253441e324ad8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 2+\\sqrt{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"92\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nFinally, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/d/75dbeb4468a2b8c9dd46834667b552f9ceac6e23.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{AB}{BC} = \\frac{2+\\sqrt{5}}{1} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } 2+\\sqrt{5}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"246\" height=\"43\" />.\n</p><p>~<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User:Zhixing\" title=\"User:Zhixing\">Zhixing</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_MOP_2024\">Video Solution by MOP 2024</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by MOP 2024\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/h92s2BxlohI\">https://youtu.be/h92s2BxlohI</a>\n</p><p>~r00tsOfUnity\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B\">2017 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 23\">Problem 23</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 25\">Problem 25</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_3\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_12_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 12 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 12 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017071106\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.074 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.102 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 845/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2298/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 158/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 28440/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   14.614      1 -total\n 57.38%    8.386      1 Template:AMC12_box\n 41.04%    5.998      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:15454:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017071106 and revision id 289988. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}